PREAMBLE

This document defines the complete technical basis for an automotive seat‑integrated, pre‑crash‑activated electromagnetic energy absorption system. The ESEMS is a passive‑eddy‑current device that reshapes the occupant deceleration time‑history during a frontal collision, reducing peak acceleration and jerk without replacing airbags or seatbelts.

Every quantitative statement in this blueprint is assigned to one of three epistemic tiers:

· Tier A – Physically established. Results follow directly from Maxwell’s equations and verified electromagnetic theory. No experimental challenge expected.
· Tier B – Analytically estimated. Derived from a closed‑form model with idealized assumptions; expected accuracy ±20–40 %. FEA and prototype measurement required for precision.
· Tier C – Design target. Hypothetical performance goal, not yet demonstrated; must be treated as a research hypothesis until validated.

The stratification is not a weakness; it is the correct posture for a pre‑experimental design.

