6. PRE‑CRASH DETECTION & ACTIVATION

6.1 Sensor Suite

· 77 GHz FMCW radar: range 0.3–150 m, update 20 ms, velocity resolution ±0.1 m s⁻¹
· Solid‑state LiDAR (905 nm): range 80 m, 10 ms update, object classification
· 6‑axis IMU (±200 g, 3.2 kHz): contact‑confirmation accelerometer
· Monocular camera (1080 p, 120 fps): object classification

Fusion runs at 1 kHz on a dedicated ECU.

6.2 Time Budget

A 56 km h⁻¹ frontal crash lasts ≈90 ms. The sequence:

Time (ms) Event
−100 Sensor fusion identifies unavoidable collision (TTC ≤ 100 ms)
−80 CPI ≥ 0.85 sustained; capacitor pre‑charge begins
−30 Lock release coil pre‑energised to near‑threshold
−5 Lock released; arrays fixed to floor
0 First mechanical contact
0 to +80 EM damping active; seat stroke exhausted
+80 Conventional restraint system absorbs remainder
+500 Spring return re‑engages lock; system reset

At 15.6 m s⁻¹ closing speed, the −5 ms trigger corresponds to a range of ~78 mm, well within radar minimum range. (Tier B for timing margin)

6.3 Collision Probability Index (CPI)

\text{CPI}(t) = w_1 \phi(\text{TTC}) + w_2 \phi(\text{TTV}) + w_3 \phi(\Delta v) + w_4 \phi(a_{\text{struct}}),

with weights w = (0.45, 0.25, 0.20, 0.10) and a sigmoid \phi(x) = 1/(1+e^{-\alpha(x-x_0)}). Activation requires CPI ≥ 0.85 sustained for ≥ 10 ms (two evaluation cycles). The sustain requirement filters spurious spikes from potholes or hard braking. False activation target: < 1 per 5 × 10⁶ km (Tier C).

